Grouper local integration patch (NOT upstream) -- apply to the
chipathon-2026-grouper submodule checkout under
lora-mimo/integration/ip/grouper/ before elaborating or simulating chip_top.

Baseline: grouper commit 3c730eb ("render GDS").

Contents:
  hw/rtl/digital_ss.sv       - add the ahb_conn_buff CPU->periph pipeline
                               register slice (closes the max_ss_125C_3v00
                               setup violator, Open Risks #1) and route
                               digital_ss's ext_ahb_m_if_* out to its port.
  hw/rtl/grouper_soc_top.sv  - expose ext_ahb_m_if_* at the SoC top instead of
                               tying it off, so chip_top's ahb_to_grp_bridge
                               has a real cross-project master to bridge from.
  hw/rtl/periph_ss.sv        - replicate ext read data across every byte lane
                               instead of zero-extending into the low lane, so
                               non-word-aligned lbu from the ext-periph window
                               reads the right byte (see
                               planning/grp-ext-periph-byte-lane.md).
  sw/src/config.h            - #ifndef-guard SYS_CLK_HZ so the integration
                               firmware build can set the 25 MHz test-chip HCLK
                               (-DSYS_CLK_HZ=25000000); UART baud divisor and
                               gtime delays are computed against it.

Apply:   git -C lora-mimo/integration/ip/grouper apply \
             lora-mimo/integration/patches/grouper-local-integration.patch
Check:   git -C lora-mimo/integration/ip/grouper apply --check <same>
scripts/run_tb_chip_top.sh applies it automatically if not already present.

